      "content": "When a white group protests a land use policy in a suburb, the coverage will likely use neutral terms like \"concerned citizens\" or \"local residents,\" framing their actions as a legitimate defense of property values. In contrast, when a minority group protests police policy in a major city, the language often shifts to \"demonstrators,\" \"activists,\" or even \"mobs,\" depending on the outlet's bias. The actions themselves might be described as \"disruptions\" in the suburban context, but \"civil unrest\" or \"clashes\" when the minority group is involved.",
